WEBVTT

00:01:51.660 --> 00:01:53.860
The EX-1 is escaping!

00:02:03.140 --> 00:02:05.040
Code 211.

00:02:05.040 --> 00:02:08.740
All enlisted men to their stations.

00:02:08.740 --> 00:02:10.610
Code 211.

00:02:10.610 --> 00:02:13.960
All enlisted men to their stations.

00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:16.050
Him.

00:02:23.630 --> 00:02:27.260
Hurricane conditions
have all fighters grounded.

00:02:27.260 --> 00:02:29.270
15 minutes until launch.

00:02:29.270 --> 00:02:30.800
SARGs are also down.

00:02:30.800 --> 00:02:32.300
Variable scanners lost.

00:02:32.300 --> 00:02:33.670
Radar lost.

00:02:33.670 --> 00:02:35.400
Auto tracer lost.

00:02:35.400 --> 00:02:37.770
The EX-1 has gotten away.

00:02:39.040 --> 00:02:40.270
Find it!

00:02:41.340 --> 00:02:43.240
We'll go to the other side
of the world if we have to.

00:03:04.130 --> 00:03:07.100
Class 5 trauma resistant concrete just like that.

00:03:07.540 --> 00:03:10.060
We'll have to cage it in something stronger.

00:03:11.110 --> 00:03:13.270
Good thing we've got our ace in the hole.

00:03:14.510 --> 00:03:16.210
Run the next sequence.

00:03:22.950 --> 00:03:24.750
Are you okay with reading?

00:03:24.750 --> 00:03:27.010
Sure, I learned from Grandpa.

00:03:36.930 --> 00:03:38.700
Dummy buildings ready for testing.

00:03:39.240 --> 00:03:41.530
Testing in city conditions, huh?

00:03:43.910 --> 00:03:45.510
Mr. Fairy!

00:03:46.640 --> 00:03:48.040
Let's go!

00:03:51.180 --> 00:03:52.480
Mr. Fairy!

00:03:53.420 --> 00:03:54.980
Not that way!

00:03:54.980 --> 00:03:56.190
To the left!

00:03:56.190 --> 00:03:57.150
Left!

00:03:59.590 --> 00:04:01.090
You can tell, right?

00:04:01.090 --> 00:04:03.960
Left's the side you hold your fork with.

00:04:03.960 --> 00:04:06.050
Your big hand!

00:04:07.100 --> 00:04:08.860
Yeah, that way!

00:04:10.330 --> 00:04:12.640
Great job, Mr. Fairy!

00:04:12.640 --> 00:04:14.140
Very nice.

00:04:14.140 --> 00:04:15.100
For now.

00:04:16.670 --> 00:04:21.180
It's been the best military strategy
since the dawn of time.

00:04:21.180 --> 00:04:24.480
Using the enemy's weapon against him.

00:04:24.480 --> 00:04:28.610
Yes, but the difference is,
this weapon has a mind of its own.

00:04:30.550 --> 00:04:32.380
Sorry for the pessimism.

00:04:35.390 --> 00:04:36.860
Stop! Stop!

00:04:42.570 --> 00:04:43.620
Bull's-eye!

00:04:46.470 --> 00:04:47.570
The next one?

00:04:47.570 --> 00:04:50.640
We have report of 920 hectopascals...

00:04:50.640 --> 00:04:52.740
...southeast of Lake Superior.

00:04:52.740 --> 00:04:54.500
Sounds like a foul afternoon.

00:04:57.380 --> 00:04:59.280
Skip sequence 3 and 4.

00:04:59.280 --> 00:05:01.480
Start short-range audio tolerance test.

00:05:07.220 --> 00:05:09.530
SARG 1, SARG 3, move in.

00:05:09.530 --> 00:05:10.530
Roger!

00:05:14.400 --> 00:05:16.230
Some drudge work, eh?

00:05:17.170 --> 00:05:21.510
Well, I thought you'd be glad
to show off in front of your rival.

00:05:21.510 --> 00:05:23.110
Knock it off.

00:05:23.110 --> 00:05:24.270
Lt. Soma...

00:05:25.840 --> 00:05:28.180
I'm talking about him.

00:05:28.180 --> 00:05:31.150
He's a rival to all pilots.

00:05:31.150 --> 00:05:32.110
Isn't he?

00:05:43.230 --> 00:05:45.130
No, Mr. Fairy!

00:05:46.000 --> 00:05:47.150
They're friends!

00:05:48.030 --> 00:05:49.430
Don't hurt them!

00:05:55.870 --> 00:05:58.270
Pull out the 3 burst automatics!

00:06:15.390 --> 00:06:18.360
Hey, Hattie. Tell him not to be afraid.

00:06:22.970 --> 00:06:25.070
Don't be afraid...

00:06:25.070 --> 00:06:26.530
It's all right...

00:06:28.370 --> 00:06:29.500
So...

00:06:33.910 --> 00:06:36.540
I hate this noise...

00:06:39.420 --> 00:06:42.520
Hattie!

00:06:45.190 --> 00:06:56.690
No!

00:07:05.540 --> 00:07:08.980
The fear lies deep in her subconscious mind.

00:07:08.980 --> 00:07:12.440
We never thought about
the reason behind it, but...

00:07:13.480 --> 00:07:16.050
...it must remind her of her lost parents.

00:07:16.050 --> 00:07:17.990
That's why I was against it.

00:07:19.020 --> 00:07:21.120
We'll arrange for counseling.

00:07:21.120 --> 00:07:22.830
That will correct it.

00:07:22.830 --> 00:07:24.230
Hold on!

00:07:24.230 --> 00:07:26.830
"Correct it"? She's not a machine!

00:07:26.830 --> 00:07:28.040
Lt. Sue Harris!

00:07:31.370 --> 00:07:35.770
We have no way of controlling
the EX-1 other than Harriet.

00:07:35.770 --> 00:07:40.440
If Dr. Noguchi and his two
staff members were still alive...

00:07:41.610 --> 00:07:44.510
...perhaps it would be a different story.

00:07:49.080 --> 00:07:51.290
Don't you feel responsible?

00:07:51.290 --> 00:07:53.390
A soldier's always responsible.

00:07:53.390 --> 00:07:54.590
That's not what I mean!

00:07:54.590 --> 00:07:57.930
If you hadn't used Harriet
to control the EX-1...

00:07:57.930 --> 00:07:59.800
...we wouldn't be in this situation!

00:07:59.800 --> 00:08:03.700
We would have been shot up
by the aliens instead.

00:08:03.700 --> 00:08:04.400
What's that?

00:08:04.400 --> 00:08:06.940
I'm sorry if I touched a nerve.

00:08:06.940 --> 00:08:08.000
It's over.

00:08:08.000 --> 00:08:10.160
Just like a hurricane.

00:08:13.010 --> 00:08:14.580
No...

00:08:14.580 --> 00:08:15.810
I don't want to...

00:08:15.810 --> 00:08:16.900
No more...

00:08:21.480 --> 00:08:22.780
Grandpa...

00:08:37.300 --> 00:08:38.360
Mr. Fairy?

00:08:42.870 --> 00:08:44.900
Yeah, where should we go?

00:08:45.940 --> 00:08:48.090
That's right! Let's go home!

00:08:49.010 --> 00:08:50.860
No one will find us there.

00:08:53.150 --> 00:08:56.400
There's a lot of places for a fairy to hide.

00:08:57.320 --> 00:09:00.450
And if we get in trouble,
Grandpa will protect us...

00:09:03.490 --> 00:09:04.760
You have your orders.

00:09:04.760 --> 00:09:07.200
We'll use patrol planes when the storm clears.

00:09:07.200 --> 00:09:10.630
Roger, we'll split up and scour the area.

00:09:12.470 --> 00:09:14.270
Hopefully, we'll find them.

00:09:15.300 --> 00:09:17.970
You sound like you don't want to.

00:09:17.970 --> 00:09:18.940
Not at all.

00:09:21.280 --> 00:09:24.850
I want level 5 protection
on the central databases.

00:09:24.850 --> 00:09:29.850
Until further notice, no one
is allowed on or off the base.

00:09:29.850 --> 00:09:30.980
Commander...

00:09:32.190 --> 00:09:33.780
This is the second escape.

00:09:34.790 --> 00:09:36.350
No one can know of this.

00:09:37.360 --> 00:09:41.820
I'll turn this base into
EX-1 Alcatraz if I have to.

00:09:55.440 --> 00:09:57.880
Yeah, come anytime.

00:09:57.880 --> 00:09:59.040
See you then.

00:10:06.760 --> 00:10:09.380
I was only helping her with her report.

00:10:14.900 --> 00:10:16.090
Believe me.

00:10:40.720 --> 00:10:42.390
You fool.

00:10:42.390 --> 00:10:45.290
Just tell me what you're
thinking from the start.

00:10:52.170 --> 00:10:53.870
A liar, huh?

00:10:55.770 --> 00:10:57.010
But you're not!

00:10:57.010 --> 00:10:59.010
You're not a fairy!

00:10:59.010 --> 00:11:00.080
You're a liar!

00:11:00.080 --> 00:11:01.780
You're a liar, and you're bad!

00:11:09.720 --> 00:11:12.690
SARG 5, please turn back.

00:11:12.690 --> 00:11:16.090
You're leaving the assigned area.

00:11:16.090 --> 00:11:17.360
This is SARG 5.

00:11:17.360 --> 00:11:19.260
I'd like to expand the area.

00:11:19.260 --> 00:11:20.230
That guy...

00:11:20.230 --> 00:11:21.530
Again with this?

00:11:23.400 --> 00:11:24.900
For what reason?

00:11:24.900 --> 00:11:26.270
None.

00:11:26.270 --> 00:11:27.500
Just a hunch.

00:11:28.540 --> 00:11:29.660
Commander...

00:11:31.670 --> 00:11:32.870
I see.

00:11:32.870 --> 00:11:36.520
A pilot who thinks his control stick
is a divining rod.

00:11:37.380 --> 00:11:38.380
I'll allow it.

00:11:38.880 --> 00:11:40.350
Are you sure?

00:11:40.350 --> 00:11:44.050
Hunches, telepathy...
I'll take anything I can get now.

00:11:44.050 --> 00:11:45.050
Roger.

00:11:45.050 --> 00:11:47.920
SARG 5 moving outside target area.

00:11:48.920 --> 00:11:49.980
And Commander...

00:11:51.290 --> 00:11:55.130
I'm not giving the monster any place to hide.

00:11:55.130 --> 00:11:56.100
Out.

00:12:53.820 --> 00:12:55.070
Grandpa...

00:13:22.650 --> 00:13:25.590
It's all gone...

00:13:25.590 --> 00:13:28.190
Everyone's gone...

00:13:35.600 --> 00:13:37.630
This is White Stork.

00:13:37.630 --> 00:13:39.530
I just found me an alien.

00:13:39.530 --> 00:13:41.590
Going in to kick butt.

00:13:47.110 --> 00:13:48.110
Woo!

00:13:48.110 --> 00:13:50.010
Blew him out of this world.

00:13:56.320 --> 00:14:00.890
Man, I'm getting sick of patrolling
this ugly, scorched mountain.

00:14:00.890 --> 00:14:03.730
The alien was here four months ago.

00:14:03.730 --> 00:14:06.130
Well, at least it's safe.

00:14:07.000 --> 00:14:11.190
The safest place in a war is one
that's already been bombed.

00:14:12.330 --> 00:14:14.770
This is White Stork.

00:14:14.770 --> 00:14:16.840
All quiet. Nothing to report.

00:14:16.840 --> 00:14:18.240
Over.

00:14:18.240 --> 00:14:19.880
Roger.

00:14:19.880 --> 00:14:23.130
Proceed to and patrol 0930.

00:14:24.080 --> 00:14:25.150
Understood.

00:14:31.620 --> 00:14:32.850
I'm all right.

00:14:32.850 --> 00:14:34.520
Thanks, Walton.

00:14:36.160 --> 00:14:37.280
An airplane?

00:14:38.360 --> 00:14:40.260
We have to hide right away!

00:14:43.300 --> 00:14:44.670
No! Sit!

00:14:44.670 --> 00:14:46.000
Sit down!

00:14:46.000 --> 00:14:47.560
Not you, Walton!

00:14:50.840 --> 00:14:53.830
The fire really cleared the place out, huh?

00:14:55.840 --> 00:14:56.810
What is it?

00:14:58.210 --> 00:15:00.610
Your safest place theory...

00:15:01.650 --> 00:15:02.950
So much for it...

00:15:10.560 --> 00:15:12.760
Bird House, alien spotted!

00:15:12.760 --> 00:15:14.530
Southwest of 021!

00:15:14.530 --> 00:15:15.630
I'm firing!

00:15:15.630 --> 00:15:18.170
White Stork, you are not to engage.

00:15:18.170 --> 00:15:20.530
Repeat, you are not to engage.

00:15:27.540 --> 00:15:28.670
No!

00:15:33.250 --> 00:15:34.220
Walton!

00:15:44.530 --> 00:15:46.050
They're friends!

00:16:09.380 --> 00:16:12.190
All right! We've got him scared!

00:16:12.190 --> 00:16:13.450
Let's finish him!

00:16:16.090 --> 00:16:17.630
In the Rockies?

00:16:17.630 --> 00:16:19.760
I'm headed for 021 now.

00:16:19.760 --> 00:16:20.960
Understood.

00:16:20.960 --> 00:16:23.000
Hold the EX-1 off.

00:16:23.000 --> 00:16:25.630
I'll send the other SARGs as backup.

00:16:25.630 --> 00:16:26.900
Roger.

00:16:26.900 --> 00:16:28.940
Well, we've recovered it.

00:16:28.940 --> 00:16:30.870
No. Not yet.

00:16:30.870 --> 00:16:34.080
I'll ask the general to hold back the army.

00:16:34.080 --> 00:16:35.210
But the secret...

00:16:35.210 --> 00:16:37.660
At least we're keeping
the wound from opening.

00:16:41.650 --> 00:16:43.140
Die already!

00:16:50.360 --> 00:16:52.720
Walton, hang in there!

00:16:58.800 --> 00:17:00.500
Crap, out of ammo!

00:17:01.770 --> 00:17:02.800
What?

00:17:02.800 --> 00:17:04.170
D-Down there!

00:17:11.280 --> 00:17:13.080
He's gonna kill us!

00:17:27.660 --> 00:17:29.460
<i>Bird House to White Stork.</i>

00:17:29.460 --> 00:17:29.600
<i>Return to base.</i>

00:17:29.600 --> 00:17:30.940
Just now...

00:17:30.940 --> 00:17:31.260
<i>Return to base.</i>

00:17:32.300 --> 00:17:36.270
Did you see a little girl
in a red dress under the alien?

00:17:36.270 --> 00:17:37.840
What are you, crazy?

00:17:37.840 --> 00:17:41.580
If there was one there, she'd be roadkill.

00:17:41.580 --> 00:17:43.570
Yeah, I guess you're right.

00:19:04.090 --> 00:19:07.230
Walton... Please, Walton...

00:19:07.230 --> 00:19:09.500
Please don't go...

00:19:09.500 --> 00:19:11.000
Stay with me...

00:19:11.000 --> 00:19:14.070
Don't go to the land of the fairies...

00:19:14.070 --> 00:19:15.900
I think you already know...

00:19:15.900 --> 00:19:18.750
...there's no such place
as the land of the fairies.

00:19:24.180 --> 00:19:25.340
Let's go back.

00:19:27.720 --> 00:19:30.310
If we don't hurry, that dog will die.

00:19:31.950 --> 00:19:33.090
Give up.

00:19:36.520 --> 00:19:40.300
There's no safe haven for you,
no matter where you run.

00:19:40.300 --> 00:19:43.290
You'd be found in no time
and ferreted out at gun point.

00:19:48.400 --> 00:19:49.370
You see?

00:19:54.740 --> 00:19:58.780
Holding onto memories because
of the pain you have now.

00:19:58.780 --> 00:20:00.480
I know all about that.

00:20:00.480 --> 00:20:02.680
That's why you came back here.

00:20:03.720 --> 00:20:05.290
But look.

00:20:05.290 --> 00:20:07.560
Nothing's here but the past.

00:20:07.560 --> 00:20:11.620
It's black and burnt and gone forever.

00:20:16.200 --> 00:20:20.100
You can't bring it back,
no matter how much you want to.

00:20:21.140 --> 00:20:25.470
The memory of what's lost is only an illusion.

00:20:25.470 --> 00:20:28.670
And that won't ever change.

00:20:30.580 --> 00:20:31.600
Ever.

00:20:33.950 --> 00:20:36.420
It's okay if you don't understand.

00:20:36.420 --> 00:20:39.270
I'm a liar anyway, right?

00:20:40.290 --> 00:20:42.160
But you...

00:20:42.160 --> 00:20:46.360
No, we have no place
left other than the base.

00:21:09.520 --> 00:21:10.920
You little fool.

00:21:16.420 --> 00:21:18.390
Let's go back together.

00:21:40.680 --> 00:21:42.820
It's out of my hands.

00:21:42.820 --> 00:21:46.220
This is too big for me to reverse on my own.

00:21:46.220 --> 00:21:48.120
But...

00:21:48.120 --> 00:21:51.030
We were lucky this time.

00:21:51.030 --> 00:21:56.500
But it may revert to old instincts
and turn on us at any time.

00:21:56.500 --> 00:21:58.100
I agree.

00:21:58.100 --> 00:22:00.370
Call it insurance.

00:22:00.370 --> 00:22:04.570
The risks are too great,
and we must plan for contingencies.

00:22:04.570 --> 00:22:07.710
You understand that, don't you...

00:22:07.710 --> 00:22:09.180
...Commander Ines?

00:22:10.680 --> 00:22:11.930
Understood.

00:22:30.000 --> 00:22:34.950
War and Escape

00:22:36.540 --> 00:22:39.040
Light sensitive photographs...

00:22:39.040 --> 00:22:43.280
...accentuate the fact that only
darkness lies behind eyes.

00:22:43.280 --> 00:22:45.180
Yesterday fades from view.

00:22:46.210 --> 00:22:48.960
Next time,
Escape and Memories.
